From f7d16bb107f2ef8e51af99e4f795f8e1d2000698 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:00:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/69] tls: certificate_sha256, a pin of the whole server
 certificate

Upstream e7ad8a875 (sing-box 1.15.0-alpha.13), carried back as it is: certificate_sha256 for
the outbound, client_certificate_sha256 for the inbound, both in base64, checked in
VerifyPinnedCertificate next to the public-key pins. A pin of the whole certificate is what
Xray (pinnedPeerCertSha256, "pcs" in links) and Hysteria ("pinSHA256") take; a public-key pin
cannot be made from it.

Pdk-Feature: backport-certificate-sha256
Pdk-Zone: core
Pdk-Layer: 01
